# fixedbugs, defect 560, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's R3; the
# ffi-pragmatist's `shim2`).
#
# Two modules each bind the same `static inline` shim of the program's own,
# the shape design.md §4.19 prescribes for a function-like macro, each from a
# header of its own. `build` compiles each in its own module's unit and
# prints 3 and 2. Until 2026-10-10 `heroes test` read both headers in one
# unit and refused it, *redefinition of 'fixedbugs_560_low'*.
use fixedbugs560/left_shim
use fixedbugs560/right_shim

function main()
    print(left_shim.low(status: 259))
    print(right_shim.low(status: 514))

test "both shims keep the low byte"
    assert left_shim.low(status: 259) == 3
    assert right_shim.low(status: 514) == 2
